From 219fc5061738dd5a0f7bfc92d3d3c9d36cd773ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jumper <wangchangran@set-hldy-llm-multimodal-worker28.mt>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:08:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(process-input): schedule grouped masks by active device
 rows

Use bounded per-expert workers for grouped masks that leave invalid rows
untouched. Read counts after the PDL dependency wait and iterate over active
rows while preserving padded storage and CUDA Graph replay addresses.
Keep zero-invalid launches and scale finalizers on their existing layouts.

Add graph replay coverage for changing counts, skew, empty experts and
recovery with int32/int64 counts and PDL on/off. Verify reference values,
untouched padding and exact eager/graph agreement. Document the capacity
contract and scheduling behavior.

Validation: 90 process-input layout tests passed on SM90; EP8 real-weight
probes completed across five decode batch sizes with both expert stages.

Co-authored-by: Codex (GPT-6) <codex@openai.com>
Signed-off-by: jumper <wangchangran@set-hldy-llm-multimodal-worker28.mt>
